WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.533
I want to go to

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.868
Ukraine now, where in the past

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.469
few hours,

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.971
the army has declared that new gains

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.173
around the embattled city of back Mort.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.541
Military spokesman says

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.143
Ukrainian units are advancing

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.245
despite a shortfall in ammunition

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.713
and personnel.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.648
One brigade says it has carried out

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.649
offensive actions

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.918
on the western outskirts of that city.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.253
Russia's Wagner

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.588
mercenary fighters say

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.623
they are also making progress

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.092
inside the city itself.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.559
Well, elsewhere,

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.460
at least one person

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.528
was killed in a missile

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.763
strike in the southern port

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.164
city of Odessa.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:31.898
It came amid

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.534
a large wave of strikes overnight

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.369
and in Crimea.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.605
A freight train has derailed as a result

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.672
of what Russian backed

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:40.740
authorities are calling

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.341
a, quote,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.944
intervention of unauthorized persons.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.146
Let's get more on

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:46.913
that from our Sam

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.182
Kiley, who's in southeastern Ukraine.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.283
Certainly plenty of developments

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.217
to talk about.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.986
Sam, let's start with that derailment.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:53.987
What else are you learning

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:57.690
Well, this

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.324
was a

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:58.858
rail link

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.827
between the two main cities

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.228
in the Crimean Peninsula.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.330
This, of course, was invaded by Russia

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.901
back in 2014 and later illegally annexed.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:08.535
It has been

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.771
the scene of Special Forces operations,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.374
psychological operations, obviously, and

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.943
perhaps part design attacks

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.878
in support of Ukraine.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.381
Now, this mysterious derailment

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:24.017
has been described as a tongue in cheek,

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.151
really description

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.120
from the Ukrainian authorities

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:27.954
as a consequence

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:28.955
of poor maintenance

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.591
or other such remarks.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.827
This is consistent with them

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.195
being somewhat coy

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.230
and mocking in terms of

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.532
when there are strikes

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.834
by their special forces

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:41.434
or drones

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.036
or other mechanisms

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.904
deep behind Russian lines.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.339
Or indeed inside

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.340
Russia itself,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.409
they don't admit responsibility.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.545
But clearly this was attacked

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.080
in some way.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.548
The railway as

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.183
resulted in the derailment.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.053
Carriages have come off the line.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.389
This is an important logistics chain.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.791
Part of the logistics chain

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.726
supporting the Russian war effort

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.695
further forward on the front lines.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.696
So could be seen

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.664
perhaps as part of the ongoing

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.200
softening up operations by Ukraine.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.436
Ahead of a wider

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.105
offensive sometime later in the summer

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:20.006
because the ground war

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.442
continues in paramount in particular,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.144
where the advance is being claimed

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.145
by both sides.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:25.712
The Ukrainians

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.013
claiming advances

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.748
on the flanks of this city

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.883
involved a mercenary group

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.617
making claims

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:31.885
about small advances

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.219
in their house to house

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.755
fighting in the city itself.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.992
No great strategic change there at all

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:39.859
as the Russians

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.061
continue their campaign in the air

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.329
of essentially trying

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.397
to get the Ukrainians

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.500
to spend as much of their air defenses

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.603
as they have got ahead of this

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.404
ground offensive,

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.139
when the Russians will obviously

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:53.773
want to try

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.141
to use their aviation

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.843
to best effect inside

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:57.810
Ukrainian territory.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.978
At the moment,

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.848
they don't risk that aircraft coming

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.082
close to the front lines

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.185
because of the capabilities

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.152
now that the Ukrainians

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.787
have in terms of their ability

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.255
to shoot down both missiles

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.357
and of course, ultimately aircraft.

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.091
Linda.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:12.992
And Sam,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.160
we saw another barrage

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.728
of missiles overnight,

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.064
thankfully, most intercepted,

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:18.965
but Russia claims

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.133
it has hit

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.402
Ukrainian military infrastructure.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:23.803
Is there any truth to that?

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.708
Probably or possibly.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.943
The fact of the matter

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.512
is that the reporting restrictions here

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:35.648
mean that we're not able to report

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:38.751
when there have been strikes by Russia

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.353
on military installations,

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.322
because that gives intelligence,

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.323
valuable intelligence

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.190
back to the Russians

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.159
in terms of their targeting.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.162
There is sometimes some delay allowed

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.497
between the attack

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.732
and when we can report it.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.734
But at other occasions, the Ukrainians

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.804
simply do not admit to any

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.907
strikes against their military targets

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:01.908
being conducted

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.944
outside of the frontline areas by Russia.

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:05.511
But clearly,

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.180
they do occasionally get through.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.615
We've seen that with some

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.383
very spectacular explosions,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:13.186
clearly important logistic nodes

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.020
or even ammunition

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.422
dumps over the last year of the war.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.891
And the Russians have made this claim.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.892
They've got no supporting

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.494
evidence for it.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.096
We know that the Ukrainians

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:23.463
are saying

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.698
that only one missile out of 30

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.267
got through to its target

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.068
and there was some debris

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.903
that killed one person

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.273
in the southern port city of Odessa.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.941
That may well be

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.876
the so-called success

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:39.012
that the Russians are claiming there.

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:41.014
Linda, interesting perspective.

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.348
Sam Kiley for us,

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.483
good to have you there on the ground

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.617
for us. Thank you so much.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.388
Well, live wheat prices fell early

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.689
after Ukraine and Russia

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.190
agreed to extend a deal

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:51.991
that allows grain

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.426
to be exported from Ukraine.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.361
Imports in the Black Sea.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.596
The agreement is critical

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.197
to the world's food supply.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.565
And it was brokered by Turkey

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.701
and the United Nations last year.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.002
Moscow says the extension

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.238
will last at least two months,

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.607
saying that period is decisive

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.009
when it comes to the deal's future.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.644
The US says that while it supports

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.147
the agreement, Moscow should in no way

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.449
be using hunger as a weapon.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.853
We strongly support the U.N.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.089
and Turkey's efforts on the deal,

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.891
which keeps global food

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:27.093
and grain prices low.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:27.760
But as

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.862
Secretary Blinken has previously said,

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.865
we should not need to remind Moscow

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:33.933
every few weeks

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.268
to keep their promises

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.570
and to stop using people's hunger

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:40.673
as a weapon in their war against Ukraine.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.710
Well, Becky Anderson, who is, of course,

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.844
a regular host of Connect

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:45.178
the World,

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.447
visited a ship carrying Ukrainian

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:48.781
wheat for export.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:49.315
She has more

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.216
now on why the grain

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:53.453
deal matters so much.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.688
An unassuming looking

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.590
port in Istanbul

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.926
with global significance.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.227
It's from here

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.795
that inspection teams

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:05.598
from Russia, Ukraine, the U.N.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:09.001
and Turkey deploy to vessels anchored

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.570
offshore

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:14.006
The ship that will be boarding

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.442
is anchored in the Marmara Sea.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:20.313
It left a mosque port in Ukraine on May

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.582
the 12th, carrying about 26,000

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.384
tons of wheat.

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:26.686
And it is one of the last vessels

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:27.754
to transit

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:30.990
under the current terms of the Black Sea.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.992
Grain deal.

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:35.962
But this vessel is actually quite low.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:36.929
So we're quite lucky

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.498
because I might have had to actually

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:39.799
climb up the side of this boat.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.334
But as things stand,

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:44.604
it's an easy it's easy access on fire.

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:47.073
These inspectors are looking for

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:50.042
any unauthorized cargo or crew.

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:50.743
Captain, we're

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.578
going to conduct the inspection

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:53.613
and we're going to start

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:54.947
with the documentation

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.016
on this mission.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:57.517
Here.

00:06:58.084 --> 00:06:58.951
Mohammed

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:01.387
is the captain of the Pacific Rose.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.357
So these are the passports, high school.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.659
And the crew is ready for a check face

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.429
Also on the checklist,

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:12.665
the shipment itself, in this case over

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:15.401
26,000 tons of wheat

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:17.737
to get here.

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.505
Mohammed and his crew

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:22.141
had to navigate through what is very much

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.277
a live conflict zone.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.912
While this is safe, eye contact

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:26.979
with control,

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:27.880
journalists control

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.483
and do this to control this area. Got it.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.617
Everything is safe.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:32.318
A contact

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:34.220
for our foreign secretary

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.689
in the corridor of the I.S.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:39.325
one is to see it, to establish

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:40.927
what it did to stumble, everything

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:44.063
it took since the beginning of this deal.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:49.202
Some 1800 ships have done this route

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:51.103
and been inspected

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:55.041
that some 30 million tons of foodstuffs

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:59.879
feeding more than 150 million people

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.014
and perhaps as importantly,

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:04.750
bringing the price of food globally

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.854
down by some 20%

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:10.823
The work of these

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:13.926
inspectors now goes on after Turkey's

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:14.994
president announced

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:17.063
an extension of the deal,

00:08:17.063 --> 00:08:19.332
meaning for at least another two months

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:22.201
the world can breathe a sigh of relief.

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:25.505
Becky Anderson, Morrissey, CNN.

